                                "sense_id": "191a7f78-041c-3ab9-b759-b82d986865b3",
                                "text": "Circus is a simple, romantic ballet, set to some suitable music by France’s Jacques Ibert, laid in a village square of placardized baroque, and dressed in costumes that suggest the saltimbanques of Picasso."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "52098c73-78aa-4058-a612-31e4a35ef141",
                                "sense_id": "191a7f78-041c-3ab9-b759-b82d986865b3",
                                "text": "1960, Henry Miller, Nexus, Obelisk Press, Chapter 13,\nAnother day my hands might wander over the keys with the felicity of a Borgia’s murderous paw. Choosing the staccato technique, I would ape the quibblers and quipsters of the Ghibellines. Or put it on, like a saltimbanque performing for a feeble-minded monarch."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d5493c47-7707-4a88-b626-e27b0771a72e",
                                "sense_id": "191a7f78-041c-3ab9-b759-b82d986865b3",
                                "text": "Outside, saltimbanques of snow were leaping up and flipping backward."
